+[[configurable-collection-implementations]]
+=== Configurable collection implementations
+
+MapStruct normally selects built-in concrete implementations when a mapping result is a supported collection or map
+interface. A project can replace those choices in `mapstruct.properties`, or in the classpath resource selected with
+`mapstruct.configurationFile`.
+
+[source, properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CustomList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.CustomMap
+----
+
+The configured class must be public, concrete, assignable to the interface, preserve the interface type parameters,
+and provide a public no-argument constructor without checked exceptions. If it also provides a usable public `int`
+constructor, MapStruct uses the source collection or map size as the initial capacity where available. Object factories
+continue to take precedence.
+
+Configuration resources are resolved only from the mapping compilation classpath. Unknown properties, unsupported
+interfaces, empty values, conflicting duplicates, and invalid implementation classes cause compilation to fail.
+Equal duplicate entries are accepted.
+
 === Using MapStruct with the Java Module System
 
 MapStruct can be used with Java 9 and higher versions.
